\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee trims losses, equity inflows eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2006\par 04:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to early trade)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Friday, undermined by weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders expect foreign portfolio flows into shares to lend support.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:25 a.m. (0455 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.6775/6875 per dollar, up from 44.71 hit at the start of trading, but weaker than Thursday's close of 44.64/65.  \par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were lower as traders waited for U.S. non-farm payrolls data for clues to which way monetary policy in the world's largest economy is headed.  \par \par \uc2 "This month continues to see steady flows from abroad which has helped the rupee, but any significant downside for the dollar will be arrested by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks, to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness, and analysts say it bought dollars in November helping India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jump more than $5.5 billion from late October to a record $172.8 billion on Nov. 24.  \par \par \uc2 State-run banks have been absorbing most of the foreign fund flows into the stock market, which has risen more than 48 percent so far this year. Foreign funds have poured in more than $8 billion this year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect demand for dollars from oil companies to weigh on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "There is certainly oil demand on the dips," said the chief dealer at a private bank, who expected the rupee to trade in a 44.60-44.70 band on Friday. Oil is India's biggest import and was trading near $63 a barrel.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061211e2c800053\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
