\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off 2-week low but cbank watched  \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2006\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to early trade)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rebounded from early lows on Thursday after traders squared off their short positions initiated in the previous sessions, but sentiment was cautious on expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At 10:30 a.m. (0500 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.72/73 per dollar, up from a near two-week low of 44.80 hit in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 It ended at a one-week closing low of 44.70/71 on Wednesday, 0.4 percent weaker than Tuesday's 8-1/2-month closing high after steady \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a bout of short covering. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced traders to cut its short positions yesterday, and the feeling is that it will enter again," said a dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence and demand for dollar from oil companies would keep a lid on the rupee and some expect the unit to trade in a 44.65-44.80 band on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks, was also suspected of heavy dollar buying in November when India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped by more than $5.5 billion from late October to a record $172.8 billion on Nov. 24.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness in global trade, analysts say. It has absorbed a bulk of the foreign investment inflows last month. Foreign funds poured $2 billion into Indian shares in November, taking the total to more than $8 billion this year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061210e2c70003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
