\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off 2-wk low as stocks scale new peak  \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2006\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee pulled away from two-week lows on Thursday, drawing support other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gains in the stock market, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped sharper gains, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 44.64/65 per dollar, up from a near two-week low of 44.80 hit in early trade and firmer than Wednesday's finish of 44.70/71, which was a one-week closing low.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again seen buying dollars through state-run banks, although not as aggressively as it had on Wednesday. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced traders to cut short positions and some actually went long dollars this morning," said a chief trader at an European bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But with regionals like the Korean won and the Thai baht rallying, the rupee turned a corner and we saw some steady stock market and export-related inflows."  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won was at a 9-year high while the baht's gains were capped at an eight-year high with regional central banks actively trying to curb gains.  \par \par \uc2 Also helping was another record closing high in the stock market <.BSESN>. The 30-share index has risen more than 48 percent this year, with foreign buying topping $8 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , demand for dollars from oil companies also kept a lid on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks. Analysts say they heavily bought dollars in November, helping India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jump more than $5.5 billion from late October to a record $172.8 billion on Nov. 24.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061210e2c70003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
