\par\par \b \uc2 Stocks lift Indian rupee to 8-\u189\'00\'BD mth closing high  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2006\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended at its highest close in 8-\u189\'00\'BD months on Tuesday, bolstered by foreign inflows to a record-setting stock market, but dealers said dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and oil importers checked gains.  \par \par \uc2 India's main stock index <.BSESN> ended up 0.5 percent at a record close, having traded at record highs above 14,000 points during the day. The index has gained more than 48 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended 0.2 percent higher at 44.52/53 per dollar, its highest finish since March 22, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 It has risen 5.6 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 hit in July, helped by strong foreign inflows. Foreign funds have bought a net $8.2 billion of domestic shares in 2006, including $2 billion in November.  \par \par \uc2 "There were good foreign inflows which could have been for the stock market," said a treasurer at an Indian bank. "But 44.50 could not be tested since we saw strong dollar purchases by oil companies and sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks, mainly to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness in global trade and contain volatility.  \par \par \uc2 It had forced the rupee down from an eight-month high of 44.35 in early November, and analysts said its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jump by over $5.5 billion from late October to a record $172.8 billion on Nov. 24.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said rupee sentiment was also helped by the dollar's weakness against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The U.S. unit held near 20-month lows versus the euro after soft U.S. data reinforced a view the Federal Reserve may cut interest rates next year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061208e2c50005w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
