\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on dollar weakness, cbank eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2006\par 04:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose on Friday underpinned by the dollar's global weakness, but gains are expected to be limited as traders are wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Firm crude oil prices <CLc1>, which are trading below $63 a barrel, could also slow the rupee's appreciation as India imports about 70 percent of its oil and higher prices usually means more demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar took a beating against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations a weakening U.S. economy will prompt the Federal Reserve to cut interest rates next year. The dollar hovered near a 14-year low against the pound <GBP=> and 20-month trough versus the euro <EUR=>.  \par \par \uc2 By 9:55 a.m. (0425 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.65/66 per dollar, stronger from Thursday's close of 44.74/44.75.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not like the rupee to rise too fast," the chief dealer at a foreign bank said, adding the rupee is expected to trade in a 44.63 to 44.73 band on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "They (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) may protect the current levels," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the rupee down from a near-eight-month high of 44.35 in early November and dealers said that was still weighing on sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee will retain a strengthening bias in the near term, assisted by a favourable trend of strong portfolio flows, JP Morgan said in a recent note.  \par \par \uc2 "In addition, a strong pipeline of inflows has been established, including equity and debt capital receipts, which will further support rupee strength over the next couple of months," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has recovered from a three-year low of 47.04 hit in July, helped largely by rallying Indian shares.  \par \par \uc2 Net inflows into a record-breaking stock market totaled $8.7 billion this year, including almost $2 billion in November alone.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -- ((Reporting by V. Ramakrishnan, editing by Ranjit\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gangadharan; Reuters Messaging: ramakrishnan.venkataraman@reuters.com; Tel: +91-22 6636-9039))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061204e2c10005h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
