\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in Sept  \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2006\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in September, data released on Monday showed, although dealers say it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadily in November to curb rupee strength.  \par \par \uc2 The data, released in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin, showed September was the fourth month in a row in which it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rupee held below 46.00 per dollar <INR=IN> for most of that period and hit a three-year low of 47.04 in mid-July.  \par \par \uc2 The data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is released with a two-month lag.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month to drive the rupee <INR=IN> down from a eight-month high of 44.35 hit on Nov. 10. It was trading at 45.01/02 at 1100 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $168.284 billion on Nov. 10 from $167.116 billion a week earlier, and analysts said the gain was mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars for rupees.  \par \par \uc2 It last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May when it bought $504 million, following on from $4.31 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, when it was acting to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed it bought a net $8.14 billion in the fiscal year to March 2006, lower than $20.85 billion in the 2004/05 year.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SNI|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061120e2bk001os\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
