\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds At 6-Mo High On Tsys, Liquidity; Rupee Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2006\par 13:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           45.34       +0.17 \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.52%       -4 bps \par  Call Rate*        7.05%       Unch \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount \par  October          INR0.7525   -INR0.0050 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     7.24%       +1 bp \par  5-Year Mifor*     7.40%       -2 bps \par  5-Year OIS*       7.13%       Unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are mid-points of bid-offer spreads.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices, which rose to six-month highs Wednesday on weak U.S. data and hopes of comfortable liquidity, may remain firm in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 Bond prices tracked U.S. Treasurys, which rose on weaker than expected retail sales data Tuesday. Prices were also helped by easing concerns on the liquidity front, as there is speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the past few sessions, thus pumping rupee liquidity in the system, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.59% 2016 bond closed at INR100.43 as against INR100.21 last close.  \par \par \uc2 "The momentum is strong for yields to go down...Long tenor bonds are especially in demand," said Anand Krishnamurthy, co-head of Global Markets, HSBC India.  \par \par \uc2 He expects the 2016 bond yield to be in the 7.45%-7.55% range by end-December. The 10-year yield fell 4 basis points to 7.52% Wednesday. Bond prices move inversely to yields.  \par \par \uc2 "The bond market is stable and is expected to remain stable. The Statutory Liquidity Ratio level of banks is somewhere near the statutory level of 25% and incremental deposits are leading to investments in gilts," BNP Paribas said in a recent note.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers added that bond prices were also helped by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  report, released late Tuesday, which said that a recent decline in global oil prices has helped minimize inflation risks.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee rose for the fourth straight session, helped by dollar buying by foreign banks and subdued foreign fund flows in local stocks, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't expect the (Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again unless the dollar/rupee slides to below 45 or 44.80," said S. Srinivas, senior dealer at Bank of Nova Scotia.  \par \par \uc2 He said further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the RBI was unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has fallen 1.8% in the last four trading sessions. Srinivas expects the dollar to trade in INR45.10-INR45.40 band in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 Pradeep Khanna, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC Bank, expects the dollar to find immediate resistance at INR45.40.  \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 15-11-06 1247GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061115e2bf00160\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
