\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee extends fall, dealers cite cbank hand  \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2006\par 04:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended its losses into a second session on Monday to end at a 2-week closing low against the dollar after dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=D3> finished at 44.9825/99 against the dollar, down 0.6 percent on the day and 1.4 percent off an eight-month high of 44.35 hit on Friday. It was the weakest close since Oct. 31, when it ended at 45.01/02.  \par \par \uc2 "There was sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which drove the rupee down to 45 against the dollar," said the chief trader at an private sector Indian bank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw importers rushing to cover their positions."  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday when the rupee fell sharply from its high. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Yaga Venugopal Reddy said on Friday the RBI monitored exchange rate volatility and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI does not have an explicit target or range for the rupee, but says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility and prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from straying too far from what it considers fair value.  \par \par \uc2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by 8.4 percent -- down from nearly 9 percent last week.  \par \par \uc2 A chief dealer at a large local company said the rupee's fall could draw more overseas investors to local stock markets, which ended at another record high on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark BSE index <.BSESN> ended up 0.87 percent at 13,399.00 points, a record close, and just off a new peak of 13,410.08 set during the day.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign buying of local equities has topped a net $7 billion so far in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061116e2bd0006s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
