\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian state banks seen selling rupees - dealers  \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2006\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with RBI comment, details, additional quotes)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Indian state-run banks sold rupees for dollars in suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen rapidly to its highest level in nearly eight months, dealers said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 At 1:55 p.m. (0825 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.61/62, having fallen from 44.35 per dollar, which was its strongest since late March. It had closed local trade on Thursday at 44.56/57 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pretty aggressive, but the rupee may settle around these levels. It's been a bit surprising, the way the rupee broke below 44.55 levels per dollar," said V. Rajagopal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Kotak Mahindra Bank  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India did not comment on the day-to-day movement of rupee, a spokeswoman said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started at around 44.40 per dollar. As the dollar gained, it forced those who had been buying rupees to unwind their positions.  \par \par \uc2 "Though we expected them to step into the markets sooner or later, the market was taken a bit by surprise by the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They (state banks) went straight for the offers on the dollar/rupee rather than showing their bids," said a trader at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks on Tuesday as well.  \par \par \uc2 Worries that a rally in the rupee may be eroding export competitiveness could have forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hand, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by nearly 9 percent compared to about 7 percent a month ago.  \par \par \uc2 When it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank normally does so through state-run banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that broadly its policy is one of careful monitoring and management of exchange rates with flexibility, without a fixed target, coupled with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. (Additional reporting by V. Ramakrishnan)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061113e2ba0006e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
