\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Down On Rumored RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2006\par 14:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           44.70       +0.15 \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.60%       -1 bp \par  Call Rate*        6.65%       Unch \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount \par  October          INR0.7350   -INR0.0500 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     7.23%       -2 bps \par  5-Year Mifor*     7.42%       -2 bps \par  5-Year OIS*       7.15%       Unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are mid-points of bid-offer spreads.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee closed lower Friday as large-scale dollar buying by state run banks, rumored to be on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a sharp fall.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that the rupee may recover some of its strength next week, but the market will remain wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.70, compared with INR44.55 at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 "With strong fund inflows expected next week, we may see a resurgence of the rupee," said V. Rajagopal, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Kotak Mahindra Bank.  \par \par \uc2 The 30-stock benchmark Sensitive Index ended at a record high of 13282.91, gaining 1.1% on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have been the main driver of the current boom.  \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have invested $7.26 billion in the year to Nov. 10, as against $10.7 billion in 2005. Since August, they have invested $4.42 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said, however, that the RBI may keep the dollar supported at INR44.50.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee fell in early trade, tracking global dollar weakness which was accentuated by large foreign fund flows related to selling by custodial banks.  \par \par \uc2 But the rupee started losing steam once state-run banks started buying, reportedly on behalf of the RBI.  \par \par \uc2 The fall in the rupee led traders to trigger stop-loss orders, which compounded the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, prices rose as inflation numbers came in lower than expectations and liquidity remained comfortable.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.59% 2016 bond closed at INR99.92, compared with INR99.86 at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Inflation in the week to Oct. 28 came in at 5.09%, down from 5.41% the previous week. A Dow Jones Newswires poll of 6 economists had expected inflation at 5.25%.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI's estimates inflation in the 5%-5.5% band for the financial year that began April 1.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers added that there was good demand for bonds from state-run banks.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds didn't react to September industrial output data showing an 11.4% rise on the year compared with Dow Jones Newswires poll estimate of 9.9%. Industrial production in August was revised up to 9.9%.  \par \par \uc2 However, despite the lower inflation numbers, economists sounded a note of caution.  \par \par \uc2 "The lower inflation numbers will not provide cheer to the markets as pipeline inflationary pressures still exist," said Shuchita Mehta, economist at Standard Chartered Bank, who expects inflation to accelerate to 6% by December end.  \par \par \uc2 Shubhada Rao, chief economist at Yes Bank, said that the industrial output numbers strengthened the case for a rate hike in January.  \