\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee checks gains on likely cbank dlr buys  \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2006\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details, quotes)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee pared gains against the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject much needed rupee liquidity and protect the local unit's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 At 2:30 p.m. (0900 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 44.84/44.85 -- off an intraday high of 44.7975, a level it last hit in late April.  \par \par \uc2 "There was some aggressive buying, likely by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , around the 44.82 levels to cool off the rupee's sharp gains," said V. Rajagopal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Kotak Mahindra Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We expected them to step in the market at some level but didn't expect them around these levels."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes at a time when liquidity in the banking system has dwindled, pushing money market rates up, and the rupee has rallied by nearly 5 percent from a July three-year low.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have poured more than $6.86 billion into domestic equities since the start of 2006, attracted by robust growth prospects in the world's-second fastest growing economy.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that a rising rupee against the dollar may dent valuations against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by nearly 9 percent, compared to 7 percent in the month-ago period.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the strength of capital flows, the rupee is gaining and that is something the Reserve Bank may not be comfortable with," Gaurav Kapur, senior economist at ABN Amro Bank said.  \par \par \uc2 "A stronger rupee, from exports perspective, does hurt even though exports have been growing fast in recent times," he added. Exports grew by 23 percent in the first half of the current fiscal year that began April 1.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June. It last bought $504 million in May and $4.31 billion in April, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par                 MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by V. Ramakrishnan)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE-CENBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061107e2b7000sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
