\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee driven off 5-month high by importers  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2006\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee backed off a five-month high of 45.20 per dollar <INR=IN> on Wednesday and ended down as traders were forced to buy dollars back following heavy dollar purchases by state-run banks and importers.  \par \par \uc2 Talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made phone enquiries in the market on prices also spurred traders to unwind short dollar positions on nervousness the authorities were concerned with rupee strength.  \par \par \uc2 The partially-convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 45.3650/3750, 0.2 percent lower than Tuesday's close of 45.2750/2850.  \par \par \uc2 "(Past) 45.25 levels, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be intolerant of further rupee gains as they may hurt export competitiveness. At a time when the current account deficit is widening, it can ill-afford to hurt export growth," said N.S. Paramsivam, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury at Essar group.  \par \par \uc2 If it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually does so via state-run banks to curb market volatility and prevent the rupee from straying too far from what it considers a fair value.  \par \par \uc2 India's current account deficit widened to its highest level since the economy was opened in 1991 in the fiscal year 2005/06. It doubled to $10.61 billion from $5.4 billion a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations of a rate rise have increased after data showed annual inflation running at its fastest in nearly three months. Wholesale prices rose 5.16 percent in the 12 months to Sept. 30, higher than the previous week's 4.77 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar/rupee is still looking south towards 45 on capital inflows, a hawkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and falling oil prices," DBS said in a recent note.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                     MARKET SNAPSHOT    Bombay Sensitive\par Index\par       <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (vs $)             <INR=IN>\par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061021e2ai0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
