\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India Rupee Breaks Key Level, May Slip Further  \b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2006\par 12:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with comments from the finance minister and an economist.)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee broke key psychological levels and fell to a 37-month low of INR47 to the dollar Wednesday on the back of soaring oil prices and a weak stock market, which triggered expectations of continued capital outflows.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's broad gains overseas also weighed on the local unit, market participants said.  \par \par \uc2 Although several analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could extend losses in the coming weeks, Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said the local unit is a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in terms of its trade-weighted exchange rate and hinted it may even appreciate depending on market conditions.  \par \par \uc2 At 0935 GMT, the dollar was trading at INR46.96, off its INR47.02 peak tested earlier in the session, a level last hit on June 4, 2003. It had closed at INR46.70 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "In terms of the real effective exchange rate (or REER), the value of the rupee is stable," Chidambaram told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee's real effective exchange rate, or its value in trade-weighted terms, is around 103, indicating overvaluation of around 3%. The rupee is considered fairly valued when its REER is 100.  \par \par \uc2 Chidambaram said the movement of the rupee also depends on demand and supply conditions in the market.  \par \par \uc2 "It is quite likely that the rupee might also appreciate depending on the market conditions," he said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Analysts Disagree \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several market-watchers believe the rupee is likely to extend losses in the coming weeks as slowing stock-related capital inflows leave it vulnerable to a further rise in global oil prices and a widening current account deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arbitraging by banks between the rupee market and the non-deliverable forward market overseas, and the dollar's broad rally against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are also weighing the rupee down, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There are a host of factors that are playing out right now," said Ashit Parekh, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at IndusInd Bank. "There's high global oil, the stock market fall, Middle East tensions, falling Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and, of course, the current account deficit."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parekh expects the local unit to keep weakening, albeit at a slightly slower pace going forward, with the dollar possibly testing INR47.05-INR47.10 over the next couple of weeks and even breaching a multiyear high of INR47.50 over the next few months.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee has fallen around 2% against the dollar so far in July alone and more than 5% since the beginning of the current fiscal year in April, mainly on the back of a worsening current account deficit and a weak stock market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's current account deficit in the fiscal year ended March 31 nearly doubled to $10.61 billion from $5.40 billion in the previous year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists expect the current account shortfall to widen further as India's strong economic growth fuels accelerated import growth and high global oil prices inflate the country's oil import bill.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investment flows into the local stock market have also slowed in recent weeks. Foreigners have halved their holdings in Indian equities to about $2.6 billion so far this year, compared with nearly $4 billion in portfolio inflows during the January-March quarter alone.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No Major RBI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  So Far  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the rupee's sharp decline, traders say there hasn't been any significant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market by the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While the RBI may be allowing the rupee to find its own level from the (current account) deficit point of view, it's possible they could come in to smooth market fluctuations around current levels if the market remains volatile," said a senior dealer at a local bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts believe the Reserve Bank of India will tolerate a gradual rupee decline in the coming months, as that could help correct the unit's trade-weighted overvaluation and make Indian exports more competitive in the global markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It (the rupee's fall) must be within the RBI's comfort zone, or else the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The RBI has enough muscle to correct (the fall) if they want to," said D.K. Joshi, principal economist at credit rating firm Crisil.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't fix any target level or range for the rupee, but sometimes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to smooth market volatility or to prevent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from straying too far from fair valuation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Judith D'Souza, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; judith.dsouza@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 19-07-06 1009GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060719e27j000hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
