\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee drops on Mideast tension, cbank quiet  \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2006\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to late morning)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee <INR=IN> remained in sight of a three-year low on Monday as escalating tension in the Middle East kept oil prices high but dollar selling by exporters checked further losses.  \par \par \uc2 Tough words by Prime Minister Manmohan Singh against Pakistan following last week's serial blasts in the financial capital of Mumbai also weakened sentiment toward the rupee, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 11:47 a.m. (0617 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 46.44/45 a dollar, 0.2 percent down from Friday's close of 46.3650/3750.  \par \par \uc2 "There is intermittent selling by exporters and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely absent," said a dealer with a private sector Indian bank, adding that the rupee may trade in a 46.40 to 46.50 range with a weaker bias.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to curb volatility.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength against the Japanese yen <JPY=> and the euro <EUR=> also pushed down the rupee. The dollar gained as investors flocked to the perceived safety of the world's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the intensifying Middle East conflict.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee touched 46.48 in early trade but pulled back as exporters sold at weaker levels. It had hit a three-year low of 46.57 on May 31 following a stock market slide.  \par \par \uc2 Worsening fight between Israel and Hizbollah guerrillas kept oil prices near record highs on Monday. India imports about 70 percent of its oil and high prices could widen its trade deficit and depress the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060720e27h0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
