\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee recovers ground after nearing 3-yr low  \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2006\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee <INR=IN> recovered ground after nearing a recent three-year low on Friday to end only marginally down, helped by exporters who sold dollars to take advantage of the cheaper rupee, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Record high oil prices triggered dollar buying in early trade but corporates began selling dollars to unwind long positions after the rupee bounced off support of 46.50 per dollar <INR=IN>, close to a three-year low of 46.57 set in May.  \par \par \uc2 "Once again the dollar failed to break the resistance of 46.50 but the trading range is beginning to go up," a trader with a private sector Indian bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 46.3650/3750 a dollar, compared with Thursday's close of 46.3050/3200.  \par \par \uc2 There was speculation in early trade that rupee demand from state banks could have been on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but some dealers discounted the possibility as rupee buying had not been strong.  \par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it usually does so through state-run banks to curb volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "Eventually, if (the dollar) breaks the resistance, the rupee could weaken very fast and touch the 47.30 mark possibly within a week," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts believe the fundamentals also point toward a softer rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee is likely to be weighed down by a steadily deteriorating current account deficit, uncertain capital flows and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's penchant for accumulating reserves," JP Morgan said in a recent research report.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar strength against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Japanese yen <JPY=>, also weighed on the rupee. The yen weakened after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) raised rates for the first time in six years but said interest rates could be kept low for sometime.  \par \par \uc2 Crude oil, which is India's largest import, surged above $78 a barrel on Friday. India imports 70 percent of its oil and higher prices push up its import bill and widen the trade deficit, putting downward pressure on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 India's trade deficit stood at $12.61 billion in the first quarter of the fiscal year that began April 1, up from $10.54 billion in the same period a year ago.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060717e27e0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
