\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slides then recovers, state banks eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2006\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee <INR=IN> neared a recent three-year low of 46.57 per dollar on Friday and then pulled back as exporters and some state banks sold dollars to take advantage of the cheaper rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the state banks' dollar sales could have been on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but others said the selling came largely from corporates unwinding long dollar positions.  \par \par \uc2 By 1:05 p.m. (0735 GMT) the rupee was at 46.40/41 a dollar, 0.2 percent down from Thursday's close of 46.3050/3200, having touched support at 46.50 in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks like \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the usual banks that sell dollars were there," one trader at a private Indian bank said, but added: "One can't be really sure."  \par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it usually does so through state-run banks to curb volatility.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar strength against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Japanese yen <JPY=>, also weighed on the rupee. The yen weakened after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) raised rates for the first time in six years as expected.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were keeping an eye on oil prices which surged to a record above $78 a barrel. India imports 70 percent of its oil and higher prices push up its import bill and widen the trade deficit, putting downward pressure on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The main stock market index <.BSESN> fell more than 2 percent on Friday due to high oil prices and weak Asian markets.  \par \par \uc2 A steep correction in the stock market at the end of May dragged the rupee down to the three-year low of 46.57 as foreign funds pulled out of shares.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060717e27e0004b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
