\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India cbank bought $4.31 bln from  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in April  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2006\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, trader quote)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 23 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had bought $4.31 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April.  \par \par \uc2 This was the third month in a row when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had purchased dollars to rein in the rupee's appreciation and maintain India's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 "It is known that the Reserve Bank bought dollars in April but the May figures should be more interesting to watch as the rupee weakened sharply due to stock-related outflows," said a trader with a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $8.15 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March and $2.61 billion in February, after staying away the preceding five months.  \par \par \uc2 In December, it sold $6.54 billion to meet the redemption of a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit scheme.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar-buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $162.876 billion on June 9, an addition of $24.35 billion in the past 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 India is the fifth-largest holder of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in Asia after China, Japan, Taiwan and South Korea.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the rupee weakened to hit a three-week low as the dollar firmed up against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will raise interest rates this month end.  \par \par \uc2 At 1:35 p.m. (0805 GMT), the rupee was trading at 45.19/20, 0.8 percent down so far in the week. In April it weakened 0.76 percent against the dollar, and hit a three-year low of 46.57 on May 31, after a sharp correction in the stock markets triggered fund outflows.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee's fortunes have broadly swayed with stock market-linked fund flows this year. Foreign funds have nearly halved their investments made this year to $2.6 billion as investors cut their exposure to emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 MARKET-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060623e26n000kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
