\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee lifts from 2006 low on cbank aid, stocks  \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2006\par 04:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee pulled off its 2006 low on Monday and erased nearly all its losses against the U.S. dollar on the back of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a partial recovery in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 45.55/57 to a dollar, off the day's low of 45.82, its weakest in 2006. It ended at 45.5550/5650 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said state-owned banks sold dollars, probably on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at various points in the day including below 45.60.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is alert about movement in the rupee related to the stock market. They are more comfortable if the swings are on account of demand-supply factors," said a dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee weakened after the benchmark share index fell by 10 percent, forcing authorities to suspend trading for an hour. The index later erased some of the losses to close 4 percent lower.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers are worried that falling shares may slow fresh portfolio investments by foreign investors and weaken the rupee further.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was in touch with major settlement banks and stock exchanges to ensure that payment obligations on the bourses were met smoothly.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement soothed sentiments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to some extent," said a dealer with a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds sold more than $555 million worth of shares in the four sessions to Thursday last week. Foreign investment of about $4 billion into shares this year has been a key support to the rupee against a widening trade deficit.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060525e25m0006a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
