\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India cbank bought $8.15bln from  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in March  \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2006\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Adds details, trader quote)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, May 19 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had bought $8.15 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March, which dealers said was to check gains in the overvalued rupee and pump liquidity into the banking system. The figures show the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in for the second month in a row to rein in rupee appreciation and maintain India's export competitiveness, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2  "We knew the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March in a big way and the data just confirms that," said a trader at a private sector bank. "Liquidity in the banking system also came back during that month."  In February the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.61 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  after staying away the preceding five months.  \par \par \uc2  Data in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bulletin released on Friday showed it bought a net $8.14 billion in the financial year to March 2006, lower than $20.85 in the same period a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2  In December, it sold $6.45 billion to meet the redemption of a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit scheme.  \par \par \uc2  The recent dollar-buying spree by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a record $162.41 billion, an addition of $21 billion in the past 12 months.  \par \par \uc2  India is the fifth-largest holder of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in Asia after China, Japan, Taiwan and South Korea.  \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the rupee headed back towards its lowest level this year as demand for dollars from oil importers and custodial banks compounded dollar gains on the global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2  Strong foreign fund inflows worth $4.2 billion -- a bulk of which have been absorbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- have helped support the rupee since the start of the year. But the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened considerably this week, tracking falling stocks and other emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2  At 2:45 p.m. (0915 GMT), the rupee was trading at 45.57/59, 1.2 percent down so far in the week and just off its 2006 low of 45.64 hit on Tuesday.    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060522e25j000qv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
