\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rebounds on cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -dealers  \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2006\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to afternoon)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee recovered much of the day's losses against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, after state-owned banks sold dollars, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 1:10 p.m. (0740 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was quoted at 45.37/39 a dollar, off an intra-day low of 45.63, but still 0.43 percent lower than Wednesday's close of 45.1850/1950.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rebound came despite a sharp fall in the stock market which rekindled worries of a possible slowdown in foreign fund inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "It is certain there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a few large state-owned banks were consistently selling dollars in the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen even below 45.40," said a dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 Indian deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rakesh Mohan said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate policy was determined by markets but it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check sharp swings.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, the rupee fell nearly 1 percent tracking weak Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after stronger-than-expected U.S. inflation data renewed speculation of further U.S. interest rate increases.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay