\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee closes near one-month high  \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2006\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, May 8 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee made a strong gain on Monday to close within sight of its highest against the dollar for a month, mainly due to dollar weakness against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  But the rupee retreated from the day's highs on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks.  \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit one-year lows against the euro and the pound sterling and a near eight-month low against the yen on Monday as U.S. rate rises were seen nearing an end, while strong data argued for a tightening in Europe and Asia.  \par \par \uc2  In the United States, weaker-than-expected non-farm payrolls data, released on Friday, sparked a widespread dollar sell-off. Most traders now expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise rates to 5 percent on Wednesday, but then signal a pause.  \par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN>, which analysts say is overvalued by 5 percent on a trade-weighted basis, ended at 44.875/88 against the dollar, up from Friday's close of 44.94/95 but off the day's high around 44.81.  \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank was clearly buying at 44.83/84 levels in the morning and 44.85/86 levels in later session," said a dealer with a state-run bank.  \par \par \uc2  Nationalised banks consistently bought at lower levels, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which aims to keep India's exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars for many weeks now to rein in the rupee. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a record $160.68 billion on April 28, a rise of $3.4 billion over the previous week.  \par \par \uc2  Money flowing out of India to cover overseas payments offset the significant impact of the dollar's weakness on the rupee, a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2  Traders will be watching India's bullish stock market, which has drawn in foreign portfolio investment of more than $4.3 billion so far in 2006. The inflow has cushioned the rupee against a widening trade deficit.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060511e2580009y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
