\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India to stay in c/a deficit in near future-finmin  \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2006\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)  \par \par \uc2 HYDERABAD, India, May 4 (Reuters) - India's current account position is likely to remain in deficit in the near future and the government will not change its exchange rate policy, Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The shortfall in the October-December quarter stood at $3.85 billion, narrower than $5.06 billion deficit in the July-September quarter.  \par \par \uc2 "Going by the current indication and projections ... India's current account is likely to remain in deficit in the near future," Chidambaram said at the annual meeting of the Asian Development Bank in Hyderabad, southern India.  \par \par \uc2 The current account registered a $5.4 billion deficit -- or nearly 0.9 percent of gross domestic product -- for the full fiscal year ended in March 2005, the first shortfall in four years.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts estimate the deficit to have widened to about 3 percent of GDP in 2005/06 as the trade gap widened on the back of a rising oil bill and as imports outpaced exports in a robustly growing economy.  \par \par \uc2 "For India, current account surplus has been a minor source of reserve accretion," Chidambaram said. "In our case capital flows as opposed top current account surpluses played an increasingly important role in the accumulation of reserves."  \par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market without any fixed target for the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "We feel that our approach aimed at exchange rate flexibility ... along with market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  essentially to manage volatililty and ebb in capital flows seems to have served us well," he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to curb excessive swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Most of the recent inflows into the booming stock market have been absorbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the rupee and keep exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have bought Indian equities worth more than $4 billion this year, adding to nearly $10.7 billion inflow last year.  \par \par \uc2 Data from India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released last week showed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $157.26 billion on April 21 from $155.196 billion a week earlier.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDIA-FINMIN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060504e254000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
