\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee tad higher on weak dlr, strong stocks  \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2006\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was held in check on Wednesday by suspected central \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after it climbed to a one-week high on a booming stock market and the dollar's drop to near one-year lows against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 High oil prices at just below $75 a barrel also restrained the rupee, traders said. India imports two-thirds of its oil and firm prices could widen the country's trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN>, which analysts say is overvalued by 5.5 percent on a trade-weighted basis, rose to 44.83 a dollar before coming off to close at 44.86/87, marginally up from Tuesday's 44.88/89 when it rose 0.17 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee rose primarily due to the dollar's weakness overseas and the stock market rally," said a trader at a foreign bank. "There might have been some light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but then inflows too were not very huge."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar eased towards a recent one-year low against the euro as investors fretted about the U.S. interest rate outlook ahead of a speech by the Federal Reserve chairman and U.S. data later in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2627 at 1217 GMT, off earlier highs of $1.2669 but up slightly on the day and near Monday's one-year peak at $1.2690.  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares rose to a new high for the third successive session, but trading was choppy as investors bought software services firms and auto makers and sold cement producers.  \par \par \uc2 Firm Asian bourses and robust fund inflows underpinned the market, which has climbed 31 percent since the start of January. Foreign funds have bought Indian equities worth more than $4 billion this year.  \par \par \uc2 Most of the inflows have been absorbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks. Data from \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released on Friday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $157.26 billion on April 21 from $155.196 billion a week earlier.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060506e2530001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
