\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on soaring stocks, euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2006\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 2 (Reuters) - The rupee climbed on Tuesday on the back of an euro that rallied towards a recent one-year peak against the dollar, and spurred by rising foreign inflows into a buoyant stock market.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said sustained dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped gains in the Indian unit.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN>, which analysts say is overvalued by a little over 5 percent on a trade-weighted basis, ended at 44.88/89 a dollar, off an intra-day high of 44.85.  \par \par \uc2 It had closed on Friday at 44.9625/9700, up 0.4 percent on the week. Banks in Mumbai were closed on Monday for a local holiday.  \par \par \uc2 "There were decent inflows into the stock market and exporters also sold dollars once they saw the euro rallying overseas," said a trader at a government-run bank. "But the state-run banks checked the rupee's rise and absorbed most of the dollar inflows."  \par \par \uc2 Traders said bunched inflows accumulated over a three-day weekend also bolstered the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rallied towards a recent one-year peak against the dollar, with strong European data offsetting earlier dollar gains made after a report the Federal Reserve chief said markets had misread his congressional testimony last week.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was boosted as euro zone manufacturing growth hit its highest since September 2000, raising expectations for upbeat language from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  even though borrowing costs should stay on hold this week.  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares surged 1.5 percent on Tuesday as strong earnings and positive news boosted drug firms and auto makers. The 30-share BSE index <.BSESN> ended up 1.46 percent at 12,218.78 points, off a new high of 12,288.51.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have bought Indian equities worth more than $4 billion this year, boosting the index by 30 percent.  \par \par \uc2 But most of the inflows have been absorbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks. Data from \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released on Friday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $157.26 billion on April 21 from $155.196 billion a week earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying spree, which possibly began as early as February, saw reserves rise by $8 billion in March. It has added nearly $6 billion to reserves in the first three weeks of April as it absorbed most of the foreign fund inflows into local stocks in a bid to keep exports competitive.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060505e2520003z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
