\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee ends higher on foreign inflows, China  \b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2006\par 05:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 27 (Reuters) - The rupee rose on Thursday aided by foreign inflows into the shares of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top oil producer, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent it breaking the psychologically key 45 per dollar mark, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee also drew support from the yen's brief rally against the dollar and the euro after China raised interest rates, they said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen tends to act as a proxy for the yuan and a rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually inspires other Asian units, including the Indian rupee, to follow suit.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN>, which is overvalued by a little over 5 percent on a trade-weighted basis according to JP Morgan, ended at 45.02/03 against the dollar, up from Wednesday's close of 45.1100/1200.  \par \par \uc2 It hit 45.40, its lowest in nearly four months, earlier in April.  \par \par \uc2 "There were some steady foreign inflows which were as usual mopped up by the state-run banks," said a trader at a foreign bank. "IOC sold some of its stake in ONGC and the inflows were related to that deal."  \par \par \uc2 Indian Oil Corp. (IOC) sold a 1.92 percent stake in Oil and Natural Gas Corp. Ltd. (ONGC) for 36.72 billion rupees ($814 million), IOC Chairman Sarthak Behuria said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Indian state-run banks usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check excessive swings by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to maintain export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the news of an interest rate increase in China also spurred the rupee, but added that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under pressure if oil prices remain high.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had raised its basic lending rate by 0.27 percentage points to 5.85 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Oil held below $72 per barrel on Thursday, after sliding almost $1 the previous day on a lower-than-expected drop in gasoline stocks in the United States. The news eased supply fears ahead of summer demand.  \par \par \uc2 Oil is India's biggest import and high oil prices are likely to widen the country's trade deficit and create more demand for dollars from importers, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 "We maintain our view of rupee underperformance given the ongoing concerns on deterioration in the current account balance," Standard Chartered Bank said in a commentary.  \par \par \uc2 "This is set to worsen further on higher oil prices. Moreover, should the strong portfolio inflows dry up or reverse, this will expose the rupee to the growing current account deficit."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060430e24r0001r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
