\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off highs as stock market drops  \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2006\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 7 (Reuters) - The rupee gave up gains to end a volatile session near a three-month low on Friday, after the stock market snapped a three-day record-setting rally and the euro fell against dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the overvalued rupee saw \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jump more than $8 billion last month to a record $151.62 billion on March 31, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN>, which analysts say is overvalued by 7.6 percent on a trade-weighted basis, ended at 44.6850/6950 per dollar, marginally firmer than the previous session's 44.7050/71.  \par \par \uc2 In early trade it matched 44.7425 hit last week, its lowest since Jan. 6 before rebounding to hit a intra-day high of 44.61.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose against the euro, recovering further from the previous day's seven-month low marked before the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  smothered market expectations for an interest rate rise in May.  \par \par \uc2 Volumes in India's $16-billion-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were on the low side as traders from the State Bank of India stayed away from work demanding an increase in their pension.  \par \par \uc2 Government-run State Bank, which has more than 200,000 staff at some 9,000 branches across the country, is the biggest player in India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets. The nationwide strike began on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "We saw some decent dollar demand from the state-run banks and it could be on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for their corporate clients," said a senior trader at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The stock market drop impacted sentiment quite a bit, leading to a fall in the rupee also."  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 30-issue BSE share index <.BSESN> gyrated in a range of 365 points, setting a record at 11,930.66 points before dropping as much as 1.6 percent to the day's low of 11,564.99 points.  \par \par \uc2 It ended 1.34 percent lower at 11,589.44 points, but was up 2.7 percent on the week.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign portfolio investments of more than $4.1 billion this year have lifted the stock index 23 percent since the start of January. The equity inflows and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans raised by companies have been mopped by the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 RECORD RESERVES, CONVERTIBILITY  \par \par \uc2 India's record \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a comfortable balance of payments situation and strong economic growth prompted Prime Minister Manmohan Singh last month to ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prepare a road map towards a freer float of the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram said in a newspaper interview published on Friday that he did not expect the rupee to become fully convertible before 2009.  \par \par \uc2 A six-person \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  committee will begin looking into the proposal from next month and will produce a road map by July 31 this year.  \par \par \uc2 "Ironically, the comment may be a modest boost for the rupee as some players had speculated that an accelerated move to full convertibility would actually be a negative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the Reserve Bank of India added to its $150 billion reserves as a safety cushion ahead of the move," ABN AMRO said in a commentary.  \par \par \uc2 "But with dollar higher versus the yen and a buy-on-dips mentality still in play for dollar/rupee, it is unlikely that rupee will see any immediate benefit."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060410e2470004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
