\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee gives up gains on cbank presence  \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2006\par 04:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 5 (Reuters) - The rupee gave up early gains to hold within striking distance of three-month lows on Wednesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has absorbed the bulk of recent foreign inflows into the booming stock market.  \par \par \uc2 But volumes were on the low side as traders from the State Bank of India (SBI) stayed away from work demanding an increase in their pension.  \par \par \uc2 Government-run SBI, which has more than 200,000 staff at some 9,000 branches across the country, is the biggest player in India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets. The indefinite nationwide strike began on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar has lost ground overseas, but here it seems the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other ideas," said the chief trader at an Indian bank. "The rupee rose to a high of 44.64 against the dollar but has given up those gains after a few of the state-run banks came and bid the dollar up."  \par \par \uc2 At 10:15 a.m. (0445 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN>, which analysts say is overvalued by 7 percent on a trade-weighted basis, was quoted at 44.6800/6900 per dollar, stronger than Tuesday's 44.7050/7150.  \par \par \uc2 If it weakens beyond 44.7500 hit last week, it will touch its lowest since Jan. 6.  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit a fresh two-month high against the dollar <EUR=>, boosted by expectations the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates next month.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also came under pressure after Kansas City Federal Reserve Bank President Thomas Hoenig said late on Tuesday that the Fed is very close to where it needs to be on policy after raising rates 15 straight times to 4.75 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the dollar's drop overseas, analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to keep the rupee competitive and also to ensure sufficient rupee funds are available to meet the government's 1.53 trillion rupee ($34.34 billion) borrowing plan that starts next week.  \par \par \uc2 Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw reserves jump by more than $5 billion in the first three weeks of March and traders say the total could touch $150 billion when data for the week to March 31 is released on April 7. India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were a record $148.662 billion in the week ended March 24.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been mopping up foreign inflows into the rising stock market and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans raised by corporates in recent sessions. The main share index <.BSESN> has risen 24 percent in 2006, helped by an influx of about $4 billion in foreign funds.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060408e2450001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
