\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds End Down On Auction, Rate Worries; Rupee Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2006\par 15:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bonds ended on the back foot Monday amid fears that that fresh bond supply will pinch money-market liquidity over the coming sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Worries that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely tighten interest rates again when it meets to decide policy April 18 also weighed on sentiment, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The liquid 8.07% bond maturing in 2017 ended down at INR103.68 from INR103.85 at the last close. Its yield closed up at 7.56% from 7.54%.  \par \par \uc2 "Players are just biding their time, before the auction announcement," said a local dealer. "Till then, bonds will move sideways. Liquidity is better, but we don't really know whether it will last."  \par \par \uc2 The federal government is set to borrow INR890 billion from the market during the first half of the current fiscal year, which began April 1, with INR180 billion planned for April alone. The first auctions are due before April 12.  \par \par \uc2 Money-market liquidity, which has been tight ever since a large capital outflow drained the system of nearly $7.3 billion in December, has improved in recent sessions on higher government spending and the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The RBI infused only INR11 billion via Monday's repurchase auction compared with a daily average of INR48 billion last week, reflecting an improvement in system funds.  \par \par \uc2 "But we need to wait and see if the improvement will be sustained. There are rate rise worries," said a dealer at a private sector bank.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its benchmark short-term reverse repurchase rate when it meets later in April - for the fourth time in a year - given the threat of high global oil prices and its impact on local inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Although latest domestic inflation slipped to 4.06% in the week to March 18 from 4.28% a week prior, it is still well above a three-and-a-half year low of 3.01% in late August.  \par \par \uc2 In the market for overnight funds, the call money rate ended down at 6.00-6.25%, from 6.00%-6.50%, previously on signs of improved system cash.  \par \par \uc2 "Mutual funds seem to have received some inflows that they've been deploying in the collateralized borrowing and lending obligation market," said a trader at a primary dealing firm. "Government spending also appears to have increased."  \par \par \uc2 CBLO's are secured money-market instruments, usually quoted below call loans.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupee ended higher against the dollar as soaring stocks fueled hopes of robust portfolio inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have pumped close to $4.0 billion into local shares so far this year following a record $10.3 billion in 2005, drawn by an economy poised to grow a robust 8.0% in the current fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended down at INR44.5950 from INR44.6200 at the last close.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar forward rates ended lower on signs of improving money-market liquidity. The forward contract maturing in March 2007 ended lower at a premium of INR0.7850 from INR0.8100 previously.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps benchmarked to the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate, or MIFOR, rose, tracking higher U.S. Treasury yields, with the five-year swap closing up at 6.67%-6.72% from 6.65%-6.70% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight indexed swap rates came off the day's highs to settle lower with the five-year swap ending at 6.95%-6.98% from 6.98%-7.00%. [ 03-04-06 1337GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Monday          Previous \par INR44.5950       INR44.6200 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums/Discounts \par June                   September                March \par INR0.220 Vs INR0.240   INR0.4250 Vs INR0.4500   INR0.7850 Vs INR0.8100 \par  \par Daily Overnight Reverse Repurchase Auction Amount \par Monday          Previous \par INR99.10 Bln    INR55.80 Bln \par  \par Reverse Repurchase Auction Rate \par Monday          Previous \par 5.50%           5.50% \par  \par Daily Overnight Repurchase Auction Amount \par Monday          Previous \par INR10.65 Bln    INR96.10 Bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Rate \par Monday          Previous \par 6.50%           6.50% \par  \par Call Rate \par Monday          Previous \par 6.00%-6.25%     6.00%-6.50% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap    6.64%-6.69%      6.65%-6.70% \par  5-Year Mifor swap    6.67%-6.72%      6.65%-6.70% \par  5-Year OIS           6.95%-6.98%      6.98%-7.00% \par  \par Benchmark Bond Prices \par Security   Maturity   Current Price   Previous Price \par  7.38% GOI   2015         98.50           99.00 \par  8.07% GOI   2017        103.68          103.85 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Judith D'Souza, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; judith.dsouza@dowjones.com [ 03-04-06 1337GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060403e243000q8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
