8.7 billion on the back of aggressive dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up rupee liquidity as capital inflows remain buoyant and export growth stayed healthy," Standard Chartered said in a daily commentary.  \par \par \uc2 "Further improvement in current account balances should help limit the risk of a sharp depreciation in the rupee. This is especially the case as we expect capital inflows to remain strong."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The main share index <.BSESN> has risen 20 percent in 2006, helped by an influx of about $3.9 billion in foreign funds. They had pumped in a record $10.7 billion, helping cushion the rupee from a widening trade deficit.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060406e2430004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
