\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves at record $148.66 billion  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anirban Nag  \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds c/a deficit, external debt, byline)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 31 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $148.662 billion in the week ended March 24 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to absorb foreign capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said part of the reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be to keep the rupee competitive on trade-weighted terms but it also served to pump rupees into the banking system to ensure sufficient liquidity.  \par \par \uc2 This in turn would help smooth the passage of the government's 1.53 trillion rupee ($34 billion) borrowing plan in the new financial year which starts on April 1.  \par \par \uc2 Steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jump by more than $5 billion in the first three weeks of March and traders say the total could touch $150 billion when data for this week is released.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves are about $30 billion more than India's external debt, which stood at $119.2 billion at the end of the October-December quarter, data showed on Friday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and it has absorbed much of the capital flowing into the booming stock market. The main share index has risen 20 percent in 2006, helped by an influx of about $3.8 billion in foreign funds.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> ended Friday at 44.6125/6225 against the dollar, 0.18 percent higher than the previous close. It hit a 2-1/2 month low of 44.7425 on Tuesday, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 Despite Friday's rise, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which analysts say is overvalued by nearly 8 percent on a trade-weighted basis, has lost 1.95 percent in the financial year to March 2006.  \par \par \uc2 HEADING TOWARDS WIDER CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT  \par \par \uc2 Other data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed India's current account deficit widened to $13.47 billion in the April-December period, up from a deficit of $5.93 billion in the same period at year ago.  \par \par \uc2 India registered a $5.4 billion deficit for the whole of 2004/05 (April-March), the first shortfall in four years.  \par \par \uc2 The widening gap was mainly due to a bigger trade deficit, which was $41.53 billion in the first nine months of the financial year to March 2006, against a $26.5 billion shortfall in the same period a year ago as imports outpaced exports in a fast growing economy.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say firm prices of crude oil also increased the trade deficit, which is estimated to end the financial year at a record $50 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Robust inflows from invisibles, which include earnings from services such as software exports and transfers from non-resident Indians, helped offset some of the trade gap on the current account. Rising foreign investments have also cushioned the rupee from the impact of the widening trade shortfall.  \par \par \uc2 "The strong corporate earnings growth over the past several quarters and expectations of continuance of (a) higher growth phase maintained foreign institutional investment interest in Indian markets," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 India's current account deficit in the October-December quarter stood at $3.85 billion, narrower than a revised $5.06 billion deficit in the July-September quarter, it said.  \par \par \uc2 The balance of payments deficit in the end of Oct-Dec was $4.73 billion, compared with a surplus of $5.26 billion in the July-September quarter.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDIA-RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|D|ABX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060403e23v000yz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
