\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee near 2-\u189\'00\'BD mth lows on dlr's gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 29 (Reuters) - The rupee dropped to near two-and-a-half month lows on Wednesday, weighed down by a firm dollar and on expectations India's central would absorb robust equity inflows, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also weaker after the U.S. Federal Reserve raised interest rates and left the room open for more increases, a move that could help boost the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At 9:30 a.m. (0400 GMT), the partially convertible rupee, which analysts say is overvalued by more than 8 percent on a trade-weighted basis, was quoted at 44.71/72 against the dollar -- near its previous session trough of 44.7425, the lowest since Jan. 6, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 It ended Tuesday at 44.6450/6550.  \par \par \uc2 "In the offshore market the rupee has weakened and so have the other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the aftermath of the Fed's outlook for interest rates and the dollar's rally overseas," said the chief dealer at an Indian bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect the rupee to trade in a weaker range for sometime and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be happy with this."  \par \par \uc2 The Fed raised rates by a quarter of a percentage point to 4.75 percent as expected and said in a statement that more policy tightening "may be needed", which many traders saw as a signal for another rate increase in May.  \par \par \uc2 Higher U.S. interest rates would boost the dollar's yield advantage over other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and could weigh on rate-sensitive capital flows into India in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said in the short run, robust foreign investment in the surging stock market would support the rupee, although traders are wary the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and absorb the inflow.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb volatility and keep exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark share index has risen nearly 18 percent in 2006, helped by foreign influx of more than $3.5 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to inject rupees into the domestic money market and ease some of the tightness the banking system has seen in the past three months.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060401e23t0002i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
