\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee at 2-1/2-month low, cautious on Fed  \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 04:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 28 (Reuters) - The rupee came under renewed selling pressure on Tuesday from foreign banks ahead of a widely expected interest rate raise by the U.S. Federal Reserve later in the session, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 An interest rate increase narrows the rate differentials between the United States and India, a factor that could weigh on rate sensitive foreign capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 At 9:20 a.m. (0350 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was quoted at 44.73/74, its lowest since Jan. 6, according to Reuters data, and weaker than Monday's close of 44.6650/6750.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar recovered from early losses against the yen to trade largely unchanged on the day as dealers awaited the result of the Fed meeting. The Fed is expected to raise the federal funds rate to 4.75 percent, its 15th straight rate rise since mid-2004.  \par \par \uc2 India's key reverse repo rate is at 5.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Financial year-end considerations are also weighing on the rupee," said the chief trader at an Indian bank. "There is some demand from the offshore forward market and we expect the weakness to continue. The fall also seems to have the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's blessings."  \par \par \uc2 India's financial year comes to an end on March 31 and companies usually rollover their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities before that date, leading to some demand for dollars.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb volatility and keep exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has absorbed most of the foreign inflows into Indian stocks. The benchmark share index has risen nearly 18 percent since the start of January helped by funds that have moved in more than $3.5 billion this calendar year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060331e23s0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
