\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases on cbank, dlr's rise overseas  \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 04:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, March 22 (Reuters) - The rupee dropped on Wednesday on sustained dollar buying by state-run banks, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit's gains overseas also undermined the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:40 a.m. (0510 GMT), the partly convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.4650/4750 to a dollar, weaker than Tuesday's close of 44.4350/4450 and off a intra-day high of 44.4550 hit in early deals according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 "They are driving down the rupee before the financial year end perhaps with an eye on the real effective exchange rate," a trader at a foreign bank said. India's financial year ends on March 31.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is overvalued by about 8.5 percent on a trade-weighted basis, analysts say. \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb sharp swings and to maintain the competitiveness of Indian exports.  \par \par \uc2 Traders are also eying companies looking to roll over foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans before the financial year ends, which could add to the rupee's weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee was also weighed down by the dollar's rebound overseas. The dollar has been rising against the euro on hopes the Federal Reserve would keep pushing overnight interest rates beyond the expected increase at next week's policy meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they would be watching foreign fund flows into the Indian stock market, but most of which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has absorbed.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have moved about $3.4 billion into the stock market since the start of January, on the back of strong growth prospects in Asia's third-largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The inflow has helped lift the benchmark BSE share index <.BSESN> about 16 percent this year, and has supported the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060325e23m0001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
