\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-India cbank wants call money in rate corridor  \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 03:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Repeat of Saturday story for local subscribers)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, March 18 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants overnight interbank call money rates to stay in the corridor between the repo and the reverse repo rates and policy instruments need to be fine-tuned to ensure that, it said in a report on Saturday.  \par \par \uc2  The reverse repo rate, or the rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  absorbs funds from the market, is at 5.5 percent and the repo rate, at which it pumps funds into the banking system, is at 6.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India said in a Report on \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance on Saturday that opening up of the economy and management of liquidity due to strong capital flows were posing a challenge in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2  "As there is a trade-off between the excessive volatility in financial markets, exchange rates and interest rates which are likely to result in erosion in the competitiveness of the economy on the one hand, and financial cost of sterilisation on the other, the Reserve Bank has to properly balance its sterilisation \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the report said.  \par \par \uc2  Sterilisation \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  had implications for the stability of short-term money market rates which called for fine-tuning of policy instruments "so as to keep call money rates range bound (within the corridor of the repo and reverse repo rates)," it said.  \par \par \uc2  Overnight interbank funding costs rose to a 3-\u189\'00\'BD   year high of 8 percent in January due to a redemption of India Millennium Deposits in late December, a build-up of cash balances by the government with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sustained credit growth.  \par \par \uc2  Overnight call money has since eased to around 6.5-6.75 percent on increased government spending and after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in which it buys dollars and sells rupees, led to some cash surpluses with banks.  \par \par \uc2  The RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through state-run banks. As it buys dollars to absorb the foreign capital inflows it releases rupees to the banking system.  \par \par \uc2  These rupees, which could fuel inflation, are then absorbed or "sterilised" by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing market stabilisation securities, the interest on which is borne by the government.  \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have pumped more than $3.2 billion into the stock market since the start of the year, after putting in a record $10.7 billion in 2005.  \par \par \uc2  The inflows so far this year have helped the rupee rise nearly 1.4 percent against the dollar but traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it down.     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK-RATES (REPEAT)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060320e23k0004o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
