\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off 1-week high on cbank, dollar eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 04:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 16 (Reuters) - The rupee slipped from a one-week high on Thursday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but managed to make modest gains on the day as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased overseas, with steady foreign inflows also lending support.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said dollar inflows had bunched up during a holiday on Wednesday and stronger regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bolstered the rupee, which analysts say is overvalued by nearly 9 percent on a trade-weighted basis.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <INR=IN> ended at 44.4250/4350 per dollar, 0.1 percent higher than Tuesday's close of 44.4700/4800. It touched 44.39, according to Reuters data, which was its highest level since March 8.  \par \par \uc2 Markets in India's financial hub, Mumbai, were closed for a religious festival on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "There were some dollar purchases by state-run banks, which we suspect was for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at around 44.39 levels," said a trader at a foreign bank. "There was also some demand from offshore investors which pulled the rupee down."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through state-run banks to curb excessive swings and also keep exports competitive, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Another trader at an Indian bank said companies were looking to roll over foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans before the financial year ends on March 31, which was putting some pressure on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing some underlying demand from corporates who have \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  liablities and that is despite the dollar losing ground against the euro," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose to a fresh 10-day high versus the dollar on Thursday, amid media reports that the next euro zone rate increase could come as soon as May.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains came after the dollar lost ground earlier in the day as the market vacillated over how long the U.S. unit can maintain its interest rate advantage over other majors.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said Indian shares, which scaled another record peak on Thursday, also helped the rupee. India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> has risen nearly 16 percent in 2006, boosted largely by net foreign fund inflows of more than $3.2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 These inflows have put upward pressure on the rupee, with only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checking gains. Analysts say if the steady pace of foreign inflows continues, it could cushion the rupee from India's widening trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Data just before market close on Tuesday showed India's trade deficit for February widened to $3.20 billion from $2.12 billion in February 2005. Analysts said the shortfall was higher than expected and could put weigh on the rupee in the short run.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060319e23g0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
