\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips as market unwilling to test cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened slightly on Monday as the dollar gained against the yen and as traders held off local deals in nervousness that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to cap any rupee gains.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers suspect the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell rupees via state-run banks last week to counter upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strong inflows of foreign funds into the rising stock market.  \par \par \uc2 They said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action so far on Monday but anticipation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keeping the rupee in a 44.32-44.37 per dollar range <INR=IN>.  \par \par \uc2 "We've seen in the last few days the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  so you're not seeing much movement," said Rohan Lasrado, deputy chief dealer at HDFC Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Volatility has come down. We are now stuck in a range because the inflows are outweighing the (dollar) demand side, which is why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is coming in."  \par \par \uc2 The rupee was quoted at 44.3600/44.3650 per dollar by 0450 GMT, weaker than Friday's close at 44.33/34.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said oil companies were bidding for dollars but dollar supply was coming from firms raising funds overseas, exporters and foreign investors putting money into stocks.  \par \par \uc2 The main stock index <.BSESN> was 0.85 percent higher shortly after the open on Monday, not far off a record high set on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The index rallied 3.9 percent last week after the government unveiled its budget for 2006/07. Foreign institutional investors have bought more than $2.7 billion worth of Indian shares so far this calendar year.  \par \par \uc2 On the international foreign exchanges, the dollar was extending gains on the day against the yen <JPY=> and struggling back from a one-month low against the euro <EUR=>.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060309e2360005r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
