\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee down slightly, sticks to tight range  \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2006\par 04:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-day)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The rupee weakened marginally on Tuesday due to corporate demand for dollars, but traded in a tight range with dealers eyeing strong foreign buying in the local stock market.  \par \par \uc2 At 12:05 p.m. (0635 GMT), the rupee was quoted at 44.39/40, marginally down from Monday's closing levels of 44.37/38 but above Friday's one-month low at 44.4975.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been some corporate buying of dollars," said a trader at an Indian bank in Mumbai. "The stock market is up again and this should support the rupee unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes into the market."  \par \par \uc2 India's key stock index <.BSESN> rose on Tuesday, as investors shrugged off worries about the economic impact of bird flu in the country and focused on strong foreign fund inflows and gains in other Asian markets.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds bought a net $77.6 million worth of Indian shares on Friday. That was the second straight day of net buying after two consecutive sessions of selling.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has not been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to weaken the rupee. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for rupees via state banks last week.  \par \par \uc2 They add that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been aimed at keeping the rupee exchange rate competitive for exporters and easing some of the tight money conditions in the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 But the government's decision late on Monday to cancel a bond sale worth 50 billion rupees, due before Feb. 22, was expected to ease pressure on dwindling cash surpluses with banks, and in turn lower the need for the RBI to pump rupees into the market through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The RBI was not in the market yesterday and I don't think they will be there today," said Rohan Naik, a trader at HDFC Bank. "There is no reason for them to pump liquidity into the market when the auction is cancelled. As the auction is cancelled, there is no liquidity moving out of the system."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060224e22l00072\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (india near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs